{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Landed\n\n[Change 1922](https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1922) patchset 2 merged at 2026-08-19 23:05:26 UTC with `LLM-Review +1` (PASS, no findings), `Verified +1`, and 0 unresolved comments. Gerrit rebased it server-side, so it is on `main` as **`6a4fd2fbb0`** — the `rebar-ticket:`, `Change-Id` and DCO trailers survived the rebase, and all seven files are byte-identical to the reviewed commit. Re-ran the suite against the real merged tip: 32/32 green in `test_snapshot_janitor.py` + `test_snapshot_docs.py`.\n\nClosing. The two causes that were out of this ticket's repair scope stay open and linked: `smart-disloyal-naga` (RC-A — the ~620 MiB-per-review ticket-tree copy on a key with no reuse, which is what actually sets the fill rate) and `itchy-arbored-peccary` (the ADR-promised byte-total backstop `_gc_pass` never implemented, plus `materialize_tickets` never calling `add_bytes`). `uninspired-gabardine-pilchard` tracks publishing the `AUTODEPLOY_DISK_PRESSURE` marker as a metric.\n\n**Operational note:** this fix bounds the *store*, not the *rate*. Root-disk growth still tracks review volume at the rate measured here; the janitor now pulls it back at 80% used instead of never. Watch `rebar/host:root_disk_used_percent` — peaks should stop reaching the 85% alarm floor. If they do not, RC-A (`smart-disloyal-naga`) is the next lever, not a further watermark change."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787180802173060001,"uuid":"cb0079ec-a860-40c5-95d2-6603e9bd3a08"}